uns with `--durations=25`, which prints only the 25 slowest phases per invocation — not every phase over the 1.0s cutoff. If more than 25 phases exceed 1.0s in a cell, the tail below rank 25 is invisible in the logs, so the log-mining mechanism cannot by itself satisfy the 'every observed phase over 1.0s' goal. The plan's 'use local timing only to resolve attribution gaps' clause is scoped to attribution, not to this completeness/truncation gap.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc8d76ff4ed3824ba","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 (\"Build a normalized inventory of every pytest setup/call/teardown phase over 1.0s from recent representative successful Gerrit Verify logs\") and AC-1","norm_id":"n3f2b8e4f7b9b6e6a","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A cell has 40 phases over 1.0s; ranks 26-40 never appear in the log and are silently excluded from the 'complete' inventory","Reviewers treat the inventory as exhaustive when it is actually a top-25-per-run sample"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a step that either runs the suite once with `--durations=0` (all phases) to enumerate the full >1.0s set, or explicitly narrows the inventory scope to 'the top-25 per-cell durations reported by CI' and records the truncation as a measurement gap under AC-6.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","d